4
00:00:54,803 --> 00:00:57,863
LOSING MOVE:
THE MOVE RESPONSIBLE FOR YOUR DEFEAT

5
00:01:09,818 --> 00:01:16,224
You have 30 seconds left.

6
00:01:16,225 --> 00:01:22,721
30, 29, 28, 27, 26, 25...

7
00:01:37,479 --> 00:01:38,673
Put up an umbrella.

8
00:01:42,551 --> 00:01:43,551
Is that you?

9
00:01:44,253 --> 00:01:47,313
I saw your game.

10
00:01:47,723 --> 00:01:49,123
One poor move ruined it.
I'm sorry.

11
00:01:50,826 --> 00:01:52,794
Fight like a man.
Never back off.

12
00:01:53,696 --> 00:01:54,958
Where have you been?

13
00:01:55,364 --> 00:01:59,232
We can chat later.
Right now I've got a favor to ask you.

14
00:02:02,972 --> 00:02:04,735
Play a guidance game for me.

15
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:08,537
Guidance game?
With who?

16
00:02:08,877 --> 00:02:12,005
It doesn't matter who.
Please, it won't take long.

17
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:20,554
Do we have to do this?

18
00:02:21,056 --> 00:02:23,718
I have a bad feeling about it.

19
00:02:24,493 --> 00:02:26,188
Don't worry. We'll win.

20
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:30,164
What kind of game is this?

21
00:02:30,165 --> 00:02:32,633
Just play as you always have.
It'll be easy.

22
00:02:36,438 --> 00:02:38,429
Are you gambling?

23
00:02:38,874 --> 00:02:40,136
It's none of your business.

24
00:02:42,811 --> 00:02:43,811
Tae-seok!

25
00:02:45,014 --> 00:02:50,077
Tae-seok! Tae-seok!

26
00:02:52,021 --> 00:02:53,021
Wait! Tae-seok!

27
00:02:53,389 --> 00:02:56,358
Listen to me.
You have to do this for me.

28
00:02:56,959 --> 00:02:59,861
You cannot lose.
Understand?

29
00:02:59,862 --> 00:03:01,329
You have to win.

30
00:03:02,197 --> 00:03:03,892
Just trust me.

31
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:05,967
I'll be fine.

32
00:03:32,227 --> 00:03:33,227
On 5 and 12.

33
00:03:38,233 --> 00:03:40,258
Your skill's improved drastically.

34
00:03:40,836 --> 00:03:42,827
It's just luck.

35
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:49,950
You're sweating.
Why don't you take your jacket off?

36
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:53,742
True dandies can sweat to death
for the sake of fashion.

37
00:03:59,088 --> 00:04:03,388
Is that so? I've only got swagger
in the winter.

38
00:04:05,561 --> 00:04:08,860
Wow, he is a tough match!

39
00:04:10,299 --> 00:04:14,258
He plays sharp.
A real pro.

40
00:04:15,671 --> 00:04:16,438
Take over.

41
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:18,838
Boss, I can handle this.

42
00:04:19,174 --> 00:04:20,174
Sit.

43
00:04:33,789 --> 00:04:35,689
On 12 and 12.
Stretch.

44
00:04:46,034 --> 00:04:48,503
On 6 and 6.
I can't hold it.

45
00:04:48,504 --> 00:04:50,165
I'll be right back.
You go on.

46
00:04:56,779 --> 00:05:00,237
Brother.
Can you hear me?

47
00:05:01,784 --> 00:05:03,752
<i>On 9 and 12.
Attack.</i>

48
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,686
On 13 and 8. Escape with a
Large Knight's move.

49
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:15,954
On 7 and 4.

50
00:05:20,602 --> 00:05:23,871
- How's it going?
- It's strange.

51
00:05:23,872 --> 00:05:26,102
- Why?
- He suddenly got much stronger.

52
00:05:26,675 --> 00:05:29,974
How come Black is
suddenly moving so fast?

53
00:05:37,886 --> 00:05:41,055
Holy cow!
What is wrong with me?

54
00:05:41,056 --> 00:05:43,650
I'm sorry. I need to
go to the toilet again.

55
00:05:51,733 --> 00:05:58,605
<i>I can't see the board right now.</i>

56
00:05:58,874 --> 00:06:00,637
Wait a bit.
Don't make a move.

57
00:06:00,742 --> 00:06:02,869
You're slower than usual today.

58
00:06:11,653 --> 00:06:14,315
Can you hear me?
Just linger over.

59
00:06:22,364 --> 00:06:24,457
No, that's the wrong spot!

60
00:06:32,608 --> 00:06:34,303
Don't put it there.
Please don't!

61
00:06:36,778 --> 00:06:37,778
Finish it.

62
00:06:45,053 --> 00:06:49,123
Brother, something's wrong.
Come out right now!

63
00:06:49,124 --> 00:06:51,592
You hear me?

64
00:06:59,201 --> 00:07:01,726
Get out of there!

65
00:07:26,728 --> 00:07:27,728
Tae-seok!

66
00:07:28,463 --> 00:07:33,134
I'm sorry.

67
00:07:33,135 --> 00:07:39,506
You little prick.

68
00:07:39,575 --> 00:07:41,375
Having a shadow player
at a gentlemen's game?

69
00:07:44,012 --> 00:07:46,503
Learn some fucking manners!

70
00:07:49,318 --> 00:07:52,987
Even the money is fake.

71
00:07:52,988 --> 00:07:54,148
You know what the 
consequences are for that?

72
00:07:55,490 --> 00:07:56,957
Please, don't!

73
00:07:59,761 --> 00:08:00,928
Quiet.

74
00:08:00,929 --> 00:08:07,234
I'm sorry, sir!

75
00:08:07,235 --> 00:08:11,439
I'm so sorry.
Please forgive us.

76
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,567
- Shut the fuck up!
- Brother!

77
00:08:17,212 --> 00:08:19,976
Brother!

78
00:08:27,255 --> 00:08:31,993
Wait! We're not done yet.

79
00:08:31,994 --> 00:08:35,486
Brother!

80
00:08:42,371 --> 00:08:45,863
Eat the stones.
Or your brother is dead.

81
00:08:56,485 --> 00:08:59,318
If you win,
I'll let your brother go.

82
00:09:05,694 --> 00:09:06,694
Start.

83
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:43,290
No takesies-backsies.

84
00:09:43,832 --> 00:09:45,266
It just dropped!

85
00:09:45,267 --> 00:09:46,267
No takesies-backsies.

86
00:09:46,268 --> 00:09:51,338
That's nonsense...

87
00:09:51,339 --> 00:09:56,276
Please let me take it back.
Just one move.

88
00:09:57,813 --> 00:10:02,416
Please...
Don't kill my brother.

89
00:10:02,417 --> 00:10:05,944
I'm sorry.
Please don't kill him.

90
00:10:07,923 --> 00:10:10,517
My brother...

91
00:10:16,398 --> 00:10:18,457
I... I'm done!

92
00:10:20,335 --> 00:10:26,273
There's one left!
Go and life are quite similar.

93
00:10:26,274 --> 00:10:28,242
One bad move...
leads you to death.

94
00:10:39,154 --> 00:10:40,154
Brother!

95
00:10:47,329 --> 00:10:51,595
Look at the true dandy stabbed to death!

96
00:11:15,023 --> 00:11:17,821
Dead stones are
removed from the board.

97
00:11:20,662 --> 00:11:23,358
JUNG Woo-sung

98
00:11:28,603 --> 00:11:31,231
LEE Bum-soo

99
00:11:33,542 --> 00:11:35,305
AHN Sung-ki

100
00:11:36,011 --> 00:11:38,172
KIM In-Kwon

101
00:11:39,481 --> 00:11:41,915
LEE Si-young

102
00:11:42,317 --> 00:11:44,979
AN Kil-kang

103
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:48,418
CHOI Jin-hyuk

104
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:01,597
THE DIVINE MOVE

105
00:12:05,006 --> 00:12:08,169
Mr. Director, I'd like to have
a couple of days' leave-time.

106
00:12:08,810 --> 00:12:09,810
Leave-time?

107
00:12:11,746 --> 00:12:15,910
I need to check the regulation.
Should be quite tight on things like that.

108
00:12:20,155 --> 00:12:23,357
You know, the Japanese police
once investigated

109
00:12:23,358 --> 00:12:27,862
a sample of 500 criminals

110
00:12:27,863 --> 00:12:32,132
and found one common point.
Can you guess what it was?

111
00:12:32,133 --> 00:12:36,237
Not a single one played Go.

112
00:12:36,238 --> 00:12:38,172
What does it mean?

113
00:12:38,173 --> 00:12:41,540
That the criminals who play Go
seldom get caught.

114
00:12:41,710 --> 00:12:43,871
The ones playing Go
seldom get caught.

115
00:12:43,945 --> 00:12:47,848
Why?
They can see the moves ahead.

116
00:12:47,849 --> 00:12:50,618
In that sense, I can say
you're one of two cases.

117
00:12:50,619 --> 00:12:53,645
Either you cannot play Go,
or are very dumb.

118
00:12:54,589 --> 00:12:55,749
A week will do.

119
00:12:58,393 --> 00:13:03,524
Win a game against me,
then I'll let you go out.

120
00:13:08,236 --> 00:13:09,362
A large group got captured.

121
00:13:12,307 --> 00:13:13,672
Is this where he got me?

122
00:13:13,842 --> 00:13:15,776
It seems so.

123
00:13:15,777 --> 00:13:18,541
It's like I'll die
stuck in this prison.

124
00:13:19,848 --> 00:13:21,008
Not quite.

125
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:26,387
Let him come near.

126
00:13:56,851 --> 00:13:58,716
A large group of stones
is seldom captured.

127
00:13:59,754 --> 00:14:04,987
Play a game with a man here.
He's quite good.

128
00:14:06,861 --> 00:14:08,795
No one's ever beaten him.

129
00:14:10,598 --> 00:14:11,860
You damn fucker.

130
00:14:16,805 --> 00:14:17,739
I like you!

131
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:21,976
Playing with the dumpsters
was getting boring.

132
00:14:21,977 --> 00:14:22,977
One more game!

133
00:14:23,345 --> 00:14:28,874
And don't forget to make a bet.
He's addicted to it.

134
00:14:30,018 --> 00:14:32,953
Please do me a favor if I win.

135
00:14:34,756 --> 00:14:35,657
Tell me.

136
00:14:35,658 --> 00:14:40,995
I want beer, cigarettes and
free time till I serve my sentence.

137
00:14:40,996 --> 00:14:44,659
You wanna play for stakes?

138
00:14:46,201 --> 00:14:47,901
Only if you'll allow me.

139
00:14:47,902 --> 00:14:49,062
Then what's your bet?

140
00:15:10,458 --> 00:15:11,458
You won.

141
00:15:16,531 --> 00:15:17,930
Request for leave-days
GRANTED

142
00:15:18,199 --> 00:15:21,327
But you get one month
in the solitary cell for being so cocky.

143
00:15:43,758 --> 00:15:47,159
<i>A game, please?</i>

144
00:15:57,572 --> 00:15:58,572
On 7 and 3.

145
00:16:03,178 --> 00:16:04,372
On 5 and 12.

146
00:16:05,246 --> 00:16:06,338
On 12 and 9...

147
00:16:32,707 --> 00:16:33,901
Who are you?

148
00:16:37,212 --> 00:16:38,474
Let me at least know your name.

149
00:16:46,121 --> 00:16:50,224
<i>Your company obliterated
my loneliness. Thanks.</i>

150
00:16:50,225 --> 00:16:52,345
<i>Look for a man named Drinking Christ
at Gwancheol when you get out.</i>

151
00:16:55,363 --> 00:16:56,363
Thanks for your trouble.

152
00:17:03,271 --> 00:17:06,638
Now that I have some free time...

153
00:17:10,778 --> 00:17:12,268
Please train me how to fight.

154
00:17:34,936 --> 00:17:36,927
Wow! Unbelievable.

155
00:18:11,506 --> 00:18:12,506
Help yourself!

156
00:18:46,608 --> 00:18:47,870
I got first prize!

157
00:19:16,337 --> 00:19:19,101
Wanna work for me
when you get out?

158
00:19:19,574 --> 00:19:23,343
I've got work to do.
Please do me one favor.

159
00:19:23,344 --> 00:19:26,541
I need some money.
I'll pay you back.

160
00:19:28,082 --> 00:19:31,985
It's me who owed you.

161
00:19:31,986 --> 00:19:33,544
I'll buy you drinks, then.

162
00:19:36,157 --> 00:19:39,888
As long as you are alive
till I get out.

163
00:20:23,738 --> 00:20:26,298
Was a tough search.
She's a real treasure.

164
00:20:26,974 --> 00:20:30,774
He had a hard time finding her.

165
00:20:41,222 --> 00:20:42,222
Two.

166
00:20:43,257 --> 00:20:44,257
He asks for two million.

167
00:20:44,759 --> 00:20:47,250
You've got 10 minutes. Test her.

168
00:20:48,129 --> 00:20:49,426
Ah, it's not enough time.

169
00:20:51,499 --> 00:20:54,127
These are <i>tsumego</i>. You know them?

170
00:20:55,002 --> 00:20:57,596
Ten minutes to solve them.
Understand?

171
00:20:58,339 --> 00:20:59,670
Black to play.

172
00:21:49,957 --> 00:21:50,957
I'm changing the amount.

173
00:21:52,126 --> 00:21:56,129
Three million.
Fuck off if you can't pay it.

174
00:21:56,130 --> 00:21:57,130
Now he wants three million.

175
00:22:02,103 --> 00:22:03,103
Wait!

176
00:22:07,542 --> 00:22:10,033
Fine. Call me when you have 
good stuff of your own.

177
00:22:23,991 --> 00:22:26,050
Go kill them.

178
00:22:28,663 --> 00:22:30,631
But bring the girl alive.

179
00:24:26,981 --> 00:24:27,981
Bring Navel in.

180
00:24:37,658 --> 00:24:39,148
Can we play?

181
00:24:40,061 --> 00:24:42,529
This is not a ladies' game.

182
00:24:43,431 --> 00:24:44,955
How many handicap stones
do you want?

183
00:24:45,933 --> 00:24:49,164
No handicap.
All in.

184
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:38,214
Master Noh, you'd better focus on training
the young now that you retired.

185
00:25:38,986 --> 00:25:39,986
Who the hell are you?

186
00:25:46,694 --> 00:25:48,855
You don't belong here.

187
00:25:50,631 --> 00:25:53,099
You're still okay, I guess.

188
00:25:53,300 --> 00:25:55,996
Don't eat too much.
I don't like chubby girls.

189
00:25:56,671 --> 00:25:59,873
Do you give boss a special service?

190
00:25:59,874 --> 00:26:01,398
He treats you too well.

191
00:26:03,244 --> 00:26:07,681
We can play a game with your 
life as bet, if you dare.

192
00:26:07,682 --> 00:26:09,202
You can get two 
handicap stones.

193
00:26:14,955 --> 00:26:15,979
Intimidated?

194
00:26:17,091 --> 00:26:20,960
Maybe I'll put a 
"special service" as a bet.

195
00:26:20,961 --> 00:26:23,953
Oh, I forgot you can't come.

196
00:26:25,232 --> 00:26:27,734
Stick to what you are.

197
00:26:27,735 --> 00:26:30,431
Using those dumb brains
of yours will make you sick.

198
00:26:33,340 --> 00:26:34,705
Don't you agree?

199
00:26:37,111 --> 00:26:38,135
Thanks for the advice.

200
00:26:43,451 --> 00:26:44,679
Damn, I surely can come.

201
00:26:50,291 --> 00:26:51,383
Good job.

202
00:26:54,261 --> 00:26:56,991
Take that kid.
Wash and feed her.

203
00:27:06,107 --> 00:27:07,540
I'm not really into parenting.

204
00:27:10,745 --> 00:27:12,110
I'm hungry.

205
00:27:23,924 --> 00:27:24,948
How old are you?

206
00:27:28,395 --> 00:27:29,395
Seven?

207
00:27:31,732 --> 00:27:32,732
Eight?

208
00:27:36,237 --> 00:27:37,727
You're ten years old.

209
00:27:39,507 --> 00:27:40,507
Your name?

210
00:27:47,782 --> 00:27:48,782
Liang Liang?

211
00:27:55,923 --> 00:27:59,791
PLACEMENT: PLACE YOUR STONE
ON THE BOARD

212
00:28:29,890 --> 00:28:32,154
Is your mom coming?

213
00:28:44,872 --> 00:28:45,998
Why?

214
00:28:47,908 --> 00:28:49,102
Dead.

215
00:28:57,518 --> 00:28:58,518
Do you play Go?

216
00:29:00,487 --> 00:29:04,651
No, Five in a Row.
Grandma said she'll kill me if I play Go.

217
00:29:11,398 --> 00:29:13,127
Are you really my uncle?

218
00:29:16,871 --> 00:29:17,871
See you soon.

219
00:29:42,062 --> 00:29:43,529
My reading ability
is off today.

220
00:29:43,898 --> 00:29:45,832
I was just lucky.

221
00:29:56,510 --> 00:30:00,537
Sir, can I play a game
with the gentleman over there?

222
00:30:02,149 --> 00:30:07,553
Mr. Cho, he wants
to play a game with you.

223
00:30:07,755 --> 00:30:09,552
You have similar ranks.

224
00:30:18,999 --> 00:30:20,364
I lost this time too.

225
00:30:26,206 --> 00:30:27,366
One more game?

226
00:30:27,675 --> 00:30:31,311
Aren't you broke?

227
00:30:31,312 --> 00:30:32,677
I think I got $500 left.

228
00:30:32,746 --> 00:30:35,237
Why don't you save it
for a rainy day?

229
00:30:37,351 --> 00:30:40,047
Then how about we play for
flicks on the forehead?

230
00:30:48,762 --> 00:30:51,890
Wait a bit.
Just one more hour.

231
00:30:51,966 --> 00:30:52,633
Have you collected?

232
00:30:52,634 --> 00:30:56,469
Of course! A bountiful harvest.

233
00:30:56,470 --> 00:30:59,238
I'm playing with a pushover

234
00:30:59,239 --> 00:31:00,807
I ripped $10,000 off of him already.

235
00:31:00,808 --> 00:31:03,476
This broke blockhead
lost his temper

236
00:31:03,477 --> 00:31:07,607
and wants to put bashes
with the knuckles as a bet!

237
00:31:08,782 --> 00:31:09,782
Sir.

238
00:31:14,321 --> 00:31:16,121
Why don't you go out
and drink while we play?

239
00:31:27,801 --> 00:31:31,430
Alright! Well...
Shall we count?

240
00:31:32,639 --> 00:31:33,673
Let's see.

241
00:31:33,674 --> 00:31:35,266
I won by half a point.

242
00:31:36,910 --> 00:31:44,817
I can see you're good at counting.
Then...

243
00:31:44,818 --> 00:31:46,410
Let me see.

244
00:31:49,123 --> 00:31:52,559
You can keep the change
as the winner's tip!

245
00:31:56,096 --> 00:31:58,030
We had another bet.

246
00:31:58,599 --> 00:31:59,599
What?

247
00:32:02,102 --> 00:32:03,694
Ten blows with the knuckles.

248
00:32:06,907 --> 00:32:14,439
You're tilting because you lost a lot today?
You're quite persistent.

249
00:32:16,850 --> 00:32:19,182
Got it.
Give me a blow!

250
00:32:20,254 --> 00:32:21,254
Then...

251
00:32:23,223 --> 00:32:25,817
Learn some fucking manners!

252
00:32:47,514 --> 00:32:48,514
Hit me.

253
00:33:05,332 --> 00:33:09,063
Are you fucking crazy?

254
00:33:09,503 --> 00:33:12,405
You fucker, where should I
put your dead body?

255
00:33:12,406 --> 00:33:15,671
The left corner or right?
<i>Tengen</i>? <i>Hoshi</i>?

256
00:33:15,742 --> 00:33:17,107
Son of a bitch!

257
00:33:33,527 --> 00:33:39,265
Untie me right now!
Do you hear me? Hey!

258
00:33:39,266 --> 00:33:44,135
What the hell!
Who are you?

259
00:33:44,771 --> 00:33:46,372
I guess you didn't 
review the game.

260
00:33:46,373 --> 00:33:53,939
What?
What are you talking about?

261
00:34:13,267 --> 00:34:17,931
You little prick.
You surely grew up.

262
00:34:18,472 --> 00:34:23,109
So what do you want me to do?

263
00:34:23,110 --> 00:34:25,340
What shall I do for you?

264
00:34:26,914 --> 00:34:33,217
What are you doing?

265
00:34:33,720 --> 00:34:36,689
Oh, I see.
Hit me! I'm not afraid!

266
00:34:41,828 --> 00:34:42,988
Two more blows to go.

267
00:35:06,119 --> 00:35:09,885
Son of a bitch.
You can go to hell.

268
00:35:10,891 --> 00:35:15,661
I'm wondering if your brother
has finished digesting...

269
00:35:15,662 --> 00:35:17,425
All the stones in his stomach.

270
00:35:21,368 --> 00:35:24,208
The game starts now.
Play with your hand, not your tongue.

271
00:35:36,116 --> 00:35:38,284
<i>Atari</i>!

272
00:35:38,285 --> 00:35:42,085
Can you just shut up and play?

273
00:35:42,789 --> 00:35:44,957
Damn, I should've noticed that trick.

274
00:35:44,958 --> 00:35:48,995
What trick?
My life's all about fair play.

275
00:35:48,996 --> 00:35:55,162
There's so many black stones.
It's like a coal mine.

276
00:35:56,003 --> 00:35:58,638
Hello? Wait there.

277
00:35:58,639 --> 00:36:01,540
It won't take long,
I'm just inside the building.

278
00:36:01,942 --> 00:36:03,609
You lied about
your rank, didn't you?

279
00:36:03,610 --> 00:36:06,909
If I were any better,
I'd take the pro exam.

280
00:36:07,047 --> 00:36:09,880
I never lie about two things.
My Go rank and my endurance.

281
00:36:10,150 --> 00:36:11,583
Thanks for the game!

282
00:36:16,757 --> 00:36:17,815
Catch that prick!

283
00:36:43,317 --> 00:36:45,318
Help me! Help!
Don't kill me. I'm only 6!

284
00:36:45,319 --> 00:36:48,049
You tried to cheat us?

285
00:36:48,588 --> 00:36:51,624
It was a fair game...

286
00:36:51,625 --> 00:36:53,659
Wanna cough up the money
or the blood in your body?

287
00:36:53,660 --> 00:36:56,322
The money, of course!

288
00:36:57,130 --> 00:36:58,324
Can I speak to him for a minute?

289
00:36:59,866 --> 00:37:01,663
What? Is he with you?

290
00:37:19,953 --> 00:37:21,250
You know Woo-seok?

291
00:37:23,023 --> 00:37:24,023
No.

292
00:37:28,328 --> 00:37:29,328
Mr. Song Woo-seok.

293
00:37:29,329 --> 00:37:31,126
Who are you?

294
00:37:36,403 --> 00:37:40,737
I know! I know, I know him!
I remember you!

295
00:37:42,075 --> 00:37:43,372
You're his younger brother!

296
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:47,480
So you're alive?

297
00:37:52,018 --> 00:37:56,622
Wow I'm thrilled.
My first time teaming up with a pro.

298
00:37:56,623 --> 00:37:59,925
Wow, look at this place.

299
00:37:59,926 --> 00:38:02,762
It's like a movie set.

300
00:38:02,763 --> 00:38:04,060
How did you meet my brother?

301
00:38:06,299 --> 00:38:07,664
You really don't know?

302
00:38:08,602 --> 00:38:12,629
We were on the same team.
Trying to survive.

303
00:38:13,073 --> 00:38:18,511
Your brother was a well known devil.
I mean, a professional gambler.

304
00:38:20,080 --> 00:38:26,542
Poor Woo-seok.
He shouldn't have died like that.

305
00:38:30,957 --> 00:38:31,957
Have you seen this guy?

306
00:38:44,471 --> 00:38:47,736
You know, I pulled out of
the league a long time ago.

307
00:38:48,041 --> 00:38:50,202
You go on your own.
I'm out of this.

308
00:38:51,878 --> 00:38:55,109
Join me if you change your mind.
You'll get the half of the profit.

309
00:38:55,248 --> 00:38:56,374
3 million.

310
00:38:59,252 --> 00:39:04,485
I am back not because of the money!
But because I want to repay

311
00:39:05,258 --> 00:39:07,818
your brother's kindness!

312
00:39:10,864 --> 00:39:14,630
I got you, right? I'm good at acting,
I know. Am I in?

313
00:39:22,108 --> 00:39:23,108
Hey, Master Song.

314
00:39:23,877 --> 00:39:28,147
What kind of Go master
plays at a place like this?

315
00:39:28,148 --> 00:39:29,843
No way! Not a chance.

316
00:39:30,317 --> 00:39:32,918
Listen. The two of us can split it.
We don't need more players.

317
00:39:32,919 --> 00:39:35,410
It gets too complicated.

318
00:39:41,361 --> 00:39:46,526
You're stubborn as a mule.
Wait, Master Song!

319
00:39:54,508 --> 00:39:57,136
Is this group dead?

320
00:39:57,477 --> 00:40:00,779
Guess I had a better luck.

321
00:40:00,780 --> 00:40:03,749
How did I let the large group die?
Damn!

322
00:40:03,750 --> 00:40:05,718
Don't tell me it's THE master.

323
00:40:06,353 --> 00:40:07,547
Excuse me, sir.

324
00:40:12,425 --> 00:40:16,418
Could you please have
a conversation with me?

325
00:40:16,763 --> 00:40:21,467
I'm not very good with conversations 
but I surely can talk with drinks.

326
00:40:21,468 --> 00:40:24,266
The bet is a bottle of drink, then.

327
00:40:26,573 --> 00:40:28,370
Please teach me a lesson, sir.

328
00:41:13,853 --> 00:41:15,286
I lost by half a point.

329
00:41:16,723 --> 00:41:21,626
You're much stronger than me.
Why are you sounding me out?

330
00:41:21,861 --> 00:41:23,385
Let's have a drink.

331
00:41:23,897 --> 00:41:29,802
Okay. Let's get "baptized
by the sacred water".

332
00:41:31,471 --> 00:41:36,101
Now I know why people
call you Drinking Christ.

333
00:41:36,576 --> 00:41:38,271
It's so good.

334
00:41:40,180 --> 00:41:43,849
Have we met before?

335
00:41:43,850 --> 00:41:45,317
Definitely not.

336
00:41:45,318 --> 00:41:46,808
What happened to your eyes?

337
00:41:48,021 --> 00:41:49,579
It was an accident.

338
00:41:51,424 --> 00:41:54,552
I also lost my eye
in an accident.

339
00:41:58,665 --> 00:42:00,155
I've got a plan.

340
00:42:00,767 --> 00:42:04,370
Just take care of the other eye.

341
00:42:04,371 --> 00:42:05,531
We can win.

342
00:42:06,706 --> 00:42:10,506
That blind belief
drives people to death.

343
00:42:11,444 --> 00:42:12,934
Will you join us?

344
00:42:22,389 --> 00:42:24,050
Thank you for the drink.

345
00:42:27,661 --> 00:42:29,356
Do the blind dream?

346
00:42:32,499 --> 00:42:35,768
Sure, mostly nightmares.

347
00:42:35,769 --> 00:42:37,737
And when you're awake?

348
00:42:40,006 --> 00:42:41,598
The nightmares continue.

349
00:42:47,313 --> 00:42:48,507
Is that your daughter?

350
00:42:51,618 --> 00:42:53,017
How does she look?

351
00:42:53,386 --> 00:42:54,386
Good and sound.

352
00:42:59,859 --> 00:43:02,225
Why don't you decide?

353
00:43:04,464 --> 00:43:06,489
What's your name?

354
00:43:07,534 --> 00:43:09,229
You can call me Big Move.

355
00:43:09,936 --> 00:43:13,337
And you can call me Agnus Dei!

356
00:43:16,242 --> 00:43:17,266
Let's go.

357
00:43:34,294 --> 00:43:38,526
Are you here, Carpenter?

358
00:43:43,636 --> 00:43:47,902
I think you're lost.

359
00:43:48,074 --> 00:43:53,569
It's been a while.
Can we talk for a minute?

360
00:43:54,047 --> 00:43:58,006
You're still drunk.
Go on your way.

361
00:44:08,128 --> 00:44:10,028
Can I have water?

362
00:44:16,970 --> 00:44:17,970
Here you are.

363
00:44:32,919 --> 00:44:36,582
Why? You thought I lost
both of my hands?

364
00:44:39,225 --> 00:44:40,658
I'm sorry.

365
00:44:44,864 --> 00:44:49,665
We were quite okay once.

366
00:44:51,571 --> 00:44:53,971
The happy ending isn't
for the gamblers.

367
00:45:06,786 --> 00:45:08,276
What brings you here?

368
00:45:12,358 --> 00:45:15,384
I'm fighting against them again.

369
00:45:19,032 --> 00:45:22,024
Then this is the last time
that I see you alive.

370
00:45:26,005 --> 00:45:27,404
Help us.

371
00:45:33,713 --> 00:45:36,748
OPENING: PREPARE FOR THE FIGHT

372
00:45:36,749 --> 00:45:40,617
I've been to the gambling parlor
run by Killer.

373
00:45:40,820 --> 00:45:42,879
It's perfectly organized.

374
00:45:43,456 --> 00:45:46,358
He's Player.

375
00:45:46,359 --> 00:45:48,827
He's good Go, but
better at acting.

376
00:45:48,828 --> 00:45:53,128
He's more like the manager
of the house.

377
00:45:53,266 --> 00:45:55,826
Gamblers around the nation
come here to play.

378
00:45:55,969 --> 00:45:59,598
They can't cheat each other...

379
00:45:59,672 --> 00:46:01,435
as everyone is better than average.

380
00:46:01,808 --> 00:46:03,605
Some games have a huge bet.

381
00:46:04,043 --> 00:46:07,774
That's the VIP room,
they take 10% of the bet.

382
00:46:08,681 --> 00:46:11,917
Player finds some rich guys
to play with him.

383
00:46:11,918 --> 00:46:15,387
Mainly the rich businessmen
or ones in high-class jobs,

384
00:46:15,388 --> 00:46:18,090
who have a lot of pride
and are very competitive.

385
00:46:18,091 --> 00:46:20,286
We got a real pushover!

386
00:46:21,494 --> 00:46:25,225
Once he traps you, it takes
less than a month to go broke.

387
00:46:26,532 --> 00:46:29,330
That snake-like old man is their
guidance player.

388
00:46:30,036 --> 00:46:32,838
He's Master Wang.

389
00:46:32,839 --> 00:46:37,609
He runs a calligraphy academy
but it's just a front.

390
00:46:37,610 --> 00:46:40,612
The monthly tuition is $500 for
children and $700 for adults

391
00:46:40,613 --> 00:46:45,107
and the minimum term length is 
3 months. So greedy.

392
00:46:46,953 --> 00:46:48,921
Great skill, though.

393
00:46:50,523 --> 00:46:54,482
That ugly son of a bitch
in the flower shirt is Atari.

394
00:46:55,161 --> 00:46:59,791
He's the collector, and runs the
illegal online gambling, too.

395
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:04,367
The meanest of all
is this one, Killer.

396
00:47:07,340 --> 00:47:09,274
Damn violent son of a bitch.

397
00:47:10,610 --> 00:47:13,238
Hey Big Move!
Can we leave him alone?

398
00:47:18,651 --> 00:47:19,651
Who's that girl?

399
00:47:20,320 --> 00:47:23,881
Damn. Attention everyone!
Open your eyes, Drinking Christ.

400
00:47:25,191 --> 00:47:29,184
Have you heard of the Goddess Bar?
25-year-old Kwon runs it.

401
00:47:29,362 --> 00:47:33,098
She turned pro at 15.
Gold medalist at the Doha Asian Games.

402
00:47:33,099 --> 00:47:35,334
World Champion in 2006.

403
00:47:35,335 --> 00:47:40,432
But she retired and disappeared
when she turned just 20.

404
00:47:41,240 --> 00:47:43,401
And ta-da, now she runs this bar.

405
00:47:45,611 --> 00:47:49,047
They call her Navel.

406
00:47:49,248 --> 00:47:51,876
Navel is another term
for a star point on the goban.

407
00:47:53,119 --> 00:47:55,986
I think she belongs to Killer.

408
00:48:00,026 --> 00:48:02,561
I need to leave after this game.

409
00:48:02,562 --> 00:48:06,064
Let's play one more.
Just as the game starts to go well!

410
00:48:06,065 --> 00:48:08,625
Sorry sir.
My wife is pregnant.

411
00:48:09,168 --> 00:48:13,798
What? Bad play!

412
00:48:17,043 --> 00:48:22,310
Well, I won this time too.
$600 each, please.

413
00:48:24,050 --> 00:48:26,075
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

414
00:48:28,988 --> 00:48:31,252
- It's your lucky day.
- I guess so.

415
00:48:35,328 --> 00:48:38,820
Hey, young man! Are you here to play?
Come and join us!

416
00:48:45,371 --> 00:48:47,396
What do you do for a living?

417
00:48:49,876 --> 00:48:51,707
I'm a researcher in school.

418
00:48:51,844 --> 00:48:57,049
Research?
You mean a professor? What major?

419
00:48:57,050 --> 00:48:57,817
Math.

420
00:48:57,818 --> 00:49:00,318
Math! Which university?

421
00:49:00,319 --> 00:49:02,412
I have a friend
at Seoul National University.

422
00:49:03,122 --> 00:49:06,353
He had a stroke
while playing mah-jong with me.

423
00:49:07,260 --> 00:49:11,430
But when I said we were
one short to play,

424
00:49:11,431 --> 00:49:13,228
he suddenly woke up
and played again!

425
00:49:16,102 --> 00:49:19,663
Anyway, great to meet you.

426
00:49:19,972 --> 00:49:22,770
You know what the most difficult
thing to do in mah-jong is?

427
00:49:22,909 --> 00:49:25,343
Nine Gates? Hell no.

428
00:49:25,611 --> 00:49:29,911
Gathering four to play a game.
Such a hassle.

429
00:49:31,784 --> 00:49:33,547
How did you find this place?

430
00:49:33,853 --> 00:49:36,021
I've been here once,
a long time ago.

431
00:49:36,022 --> 00:49:39,355
I don't recall your face. I'm quite good
at remembering faces.

432
00:49:43,062 --> 00:49:44,962
I was very different back then.

433
00:49:56,242 --> 00:49:57,368
You play Go, too?

434
00:49:58,644 --> 00:49:59,644
More as a hobby.

435
00:50:01,547 --> 00:50:05,813
I also play it a bit.
Let's play together someday.

436
00:50:13,159 --> 00:50:15,059
Have we met before?

437
00:50:17,630 --> 00:50:18,630
Well...

438
00:50:22,435 --> 00:50:23,595
Thanks for the talk.

439
00:50:50,930 --> 00:50:54,058
I can't do it!

440
00:50:55,635 --> 00:50:57,769
What is Carpenter doing?

441
00:50:57,770 --> 00:50:58,794
Making a chair?

442
00:51:01,674 --> 00:51:02,674
Give it to me.

443
00:51:03,910 --> 00:51:08,506
Wow, you can make
this kinda stuff, too!

444
00:51:11,684 --> 00:51:14,553
You look a bit awkward.

445
00:51:14,554 --> 00:51:17,682
What can you see?

446
00:51:18,958 --> 00:51:20,158
Driver's License
YOOK Jong-duck

447
00:51:26,465 --> 00:51:31,459
6 Ducks Entertainment!
Feels... sexy.

448
00:51:43,883 --> 00:51:45,817
Lost again!

449
00:51:48,721 --> 00:51:49,949
This seat is unlucky!

450
00:51:57,797 --> 00:52:00,265
This seat too! And this, too!
I'm getting ripped off!

451
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:01,894
Where is the lucky seat?

452
00:52:02,602 --> 00:52:06,766
Hey, the cigarettes!

453
00:52:10,610 --> 00:52:12,942
- One more game!
- No problem!

454
00:52:13,379 --> 00:52:17,115
You don't have 1 millimeter?
You wanna suffocate me

455
00:52:17,116 --> 00:52:20,051
with nicotine?
One more game!

456
00:52:22,421 --> 00:52:24,082
You have it all!

457
00:52:25,091 --> 00:52:27,218
- One more game. Wait here. Don't move!
- I won't.

458
00:52:27,827 --> 00:52:28,827
Wait right there!

459
00:52:29,328 --> 00:52:30,328
I need some money.

460
00:52:47,013 --> 00:52:51,746
You don't look like
the brainy type.

461
00:52:52,818 --> 00:52:57,084
You can tell?
Then you're in the wrong job.

462
00:53:08,834 --> 00:53:12,531
My brain cells are all dead!

463
00:53:24,984 --> 00:53:27,885
- What does he do?
- He makes adult films.

464
00:53:30,289 --> 00:53:31,289
How much did he spend?

465
00:53:31,424 --> 00:53:35,593
Hundred thousand.
Low skill, but high in pride.

466
00:53:35,594 --> 00:53:39,724
A perfect target.

467
00:53:41,734 --> 00:53:45,236
HAENGMA: SHAPE OF THE STONES

468
00:53:45,237 --> 00:53:48,900
Carpenter, did test this out?
You didn't do a lousy job, did you?

469
00:53:50,843 --> 00:53:55,041
I need a bonus
for risking my life.

470
00:53:57,316 --> 00:54:00,376
The smoking will kill me
even if I don't get stabbed.

471
00:54:04,590 --> 00:54:07,957
Stop drinking!
How can you play?

472
00:54:08,060 --> 00:54:10,961
<i>Kyu</i> player worries much.

473
00:54:13,666 --> 00:54:16,726
What if I'm a
master in disguise?

474
00:54:16,969 --> 00:54:20,372
I sometimes think so, seeing you

475
00:54:20,373 --> 00:54:22,341
treat the world
as a playground.

476
00:54:22,975 --> 00:54:26,211
The world is a playground
for the <i>dans</i>...

477
00:54:26,212 --> 00:54:29,113
and a living hell
for the <i>kyus</i>.

478
00:54:32,752 --> 00:54:35,253
That makes me
the lowest of the low.

479
00:54:35,254 --> 00:54:37,484
For me, the world
is an endless hell.

480
00:54:58,043 --> 00:55:00,705
Go for a fast attack. Divide
wedge through the center of the left.

481
00:55:06,786 --> 00:55:08,344
Approaching on 3 and 6.

482
00:55:10,656 --> 00:55:11,816
Lower Pincer by one space.

483
00:55:14,193 --> 00:55:15,421
On 12 and 12.

484
00:55:23,969 --> 00:55:24,969
On 16 and 9.

485
00:55:27,873 --> 00:55:28,873
On 10 and 9.

486
00:55:37,550 --> 00:55:39,177
Good job.

487
00:55:59,505 --> 00:56:02,201
Hey!
Search this bastard.

488
00:56:03,042 --> 00:56:04,236
What are you talking about?

489
00:56:04,977 --> 00:56:08,246
You lost one game, so you lose your 
temper too? I've lost enough here!

490
00:56:08,247 --> 00:56:12,343
Let go of me, shitheads!

491
00:56:21,894 --> 00:56:28,231
Nothing? Wow! I'm clear. Poor you!

492
00:56:29,335 --> 00:56:31,836
Losing is painful!
You see now?

493
00:56:31,837 --> 00:56:34,239
You petty bastard!

494
00:56:34,240 --> 00:56:39,200
I will kill you, son of a bitch!
You're dead!

495
00:56:42,348 --> 00:56:43,348
What the hell are you doing?

496
00:56:47,753 --> 00:56:52,349
Mind your own boards!
Mind your own games, I said!

497
00:56:55,961 --> 00:56:56,961
Sir.

498
00:57:04,703 --> 00:57:10,608
- Would you have a game with me?
- I'm not in the mood.

499
00:57:10,609 --> 00:57:13,511
Don't let a petty bastard
ruin your mood.

500
00:57:13,512 --> 00:57:14,646
What's your rank?

501
00:57:14,647 --> 00:57:17,844
What matters is not the rank,
but the condition of the day.

502
00:57:19,885 --> 00:57:22,945
Right, just like sex!

503
00:57:23,556 --> 00:57:25,790
Let me get some fresh air first.

504
00:57:25,791 --> 00:57:26,791
Sure.

505
00:57:48,080 --> 00:57:49,104
I hate cigarettes.

506
00:57:54,053 --> 00:57:57,121
Have I told you
how much I'm amazed

507
00:57:57,122 --> 00:58:00,614
by your marvelous survival skills?

508
00:58:00,693 --> 00:58:01,693
Speak for yourself.

509
00:58:02,194 --> 00:58:05,029
There aren't many options
for low-lifes like us.

510
00:58:05,030 --> 00:58:07,430
I'm not like you.

511
00:58:08,033 --> 00:58:10,331
I'm playing on the center stage.

512
00:58:10,936 --> 00:58:14,030
We're in different leagues, dude.

513
00:58:14,406 --> 00:58:20,140
Center or corner, the last man
standing takes the pot.

514
00:58:25,884 --> 00:58:28,114
A hell of disguise...

515
00:58:30,556 --> 00:58:34,822
Fuck off!
Such a rat.

516
00:58:37,529 --> 00:58:39,258
Here we are again.

517
00:58:41,000 --> 00:58:43,264
We're meant to
live like this, I guess.

518
00:58:43,602 --> 00:58:45,536
Have you ever seen a divine move?

519
00:58:45,537 --> 00:58:47,801
No, I haven't.

520
00:58:48,240 --> 00:58:54,245
Is there such a move, in life?

521
00:58:54,246 --> 00:59:00,251
A move so powerful that it can change
our life so dramatically.

522
00:59:00,252 --> 00:59:02,720
Only God knows.

523
00:59:03,489 --> 00:59:07,448
What would you do with
such a move?

524
00:59:08,193 --> 00:59:09,990
I would save your arm.

525
00:59:12,197 --> 00:59:14,097
And my wife.

526
00:59:16,835 --> 00:59:18,860
I can think of a better move.

527
00:59:22,641 --> 00:59:24,871
Go back to when you 
didn't play for money.

528
00:59:28,447 --> 00:59:29,447
I won.

529
00:59:30,282 --> 00:59:35,420
Congratulations.
It's your lucky day.

530
00:59:35,421 --> 00:59:37,722
I'm done here.

531
00:59:37,723 --> 00:59:41,192
Again today?
My luck's finally here!

532
00:59:41,193 --> 00:59:43,094
It's my wedding anniversary.

533
00:59:43,095 --> 00:59:46,622
Damn the anniversaries.

534
00:59:51,336 --> 00:59:55,238
Mister! Come join us.

535
01:00:00,879 --> 01:00:04,975
How can you make a living
if you quit teaching?

536
01:00:06,485 --> 01:00:07,816
I'm building a program.

537
01:00:08,320 --> 01:00:10,321
A program? What kind?

538
01:00:10,322 --> 01:00:12,523
A kind of algorithm for Go.

539
01:00:12,524 --> 01:00:15,152
Alg... what?

540
01:00:15,427 --> 01:00:18,896
A computer program
that can beat humans

541
01:00:18,897 --> 01:00:20,565
at Go.

542
01:00:20,566 --> 01:00:26,537
What's the point for computers
to be good at Go?

543
01:00:26,538 --> 01:00:29,564
Like it's not hard enough for us.

544
01:00:37,983 --> 01:00:38,983
I won.

545
01:00:40,819 --> 01:00:46,491
What the shit?
Nine Gates?

546
01:00:46,492 --> 01:00:50,762
It's once-in-a-lifetime luck!
Congratulations, really.

547
01:00:50,763 --> 01:00:55,466
Thank you.
Let me buy you dinner.

548
01:00:55,467 --> 01:00:58,095
Of course, you should!

549
01:00:59,671 --> 01:01:04,131
I have to go, sorry.

550
01:01:09,047 --> 01:01:11,682
You shouldn't go home today.

551
01:01:11,683 --> 01:01:14,018
It'd bring you bad luck.
You should play all night.

552
01:01:14,019 --> 01:01:19,090
Where should we go?
I know a good lamb place.

553
01:01:19,091 --> 01:01:20,422
You'd better go home.

554
01:01:23,662 --> 01:01:27,723
I won first.
But I passed for you.

555
01:01:31,870 --> 01:01:35,139
- I didn't know that.
- You better watch out.

556
01:01:35,140 --> 01:01:40,009
You had once-in-a-lifetime luck today.
You might die soon.

557
01:01:41,213 --> 01:01:44,081
I'm dead already.

558
01:01:44,082 --> 01:01:45,879
I've got no more life to lose.

559
01:01:48,120 --> 01:01:50,486
Caller ID: Killer

560
01:01:52,891 --> 01:01:53,891
Hello.

561
01:02:01,700 --> 01:02:02,700
What is he?

562
01:02:03,402 --> 01:02:04,767
He really is a programmer.

563
01:02:05,637 --> 01:02:08,406
His hands look too rough
for a computer guy.

564
01:02:08,407 --> 01:02:11,209
Maybe he smashes keyboards
when he's pissed off.

565
01:02:11,210 --> 01:02:14,304
You feel like joking?
I guess the date was fun.

566
01:02:15,747 --> 01:02:18,583
Partners shouldn't have secrets.

567
01:02:18,584 --> 01:02:20,745
No partnership is eternal.

568
01:02:21,320 --> 01:02:26,791
And your bad fortune this year
could affect the business.

569
01:02:26,792 --> 01:02:30,294
I saved your mother.
Are you forgetting the terms?

570
01:02:30,295 --> 01:02:34,131
It's a lifetime deal.
It terminates when you die.

571
01:02:34,132 --> 01:02:38,364
You never know.
Your death could also terminate it.

572
01:02:39,671 --> 01:02:42,936
Your endgame is riddled
with bad moves.

573
01:02:48,180 --> 01:02:52,283
Don't try so hard.
You're a ladder.

574
01:02:52,284 --> 01:02:56,015
You'll end up dead
no matter how long you chase it for.

575
01:02:58,790 --> 01:03:03,124
Look for the ladder breaker
before you kill. You could miss it.

576
01:03:06,265 --> 01:03:09,860
A common mistake for <i>kyus</i>.

577
01:03:18,844 --> 01:03:21,677
It's not easy...

578
01:03:22,714 --> 01:03:25,842
Hopeless bastard.
How did it go?

579
01:03:26,018 --> 01:03:30,455
What keeps you so busy?
Share some of the fun stuff with us!

580
01:03:31,623 --> 01:03:32,954
How was it today?

581
01:03:33,592 --> 01:03:36,394
Christ had a hell of a good move.

582
01:03:36,395 --> 01:03:39,831
Masters never hesitate.

583
01:03:39,965 --> 01:03:40,965
Go by yourself tomorrow.

584
01:03:41,934 --> 01:03:44,468
You want me to walk into 
the lion's den alone?

585
01:03:44,469 --> 01:03:46,869
Don't worry.
He'll let you win.

586
01:03:49,541 --> 01:03:53,409
What does that mean?
Hey, tell me!

587
01:04:02,321 --> 01:04:05,654
Today's not the day for me.
Thanks for a good game.

588
01:04:07,359 --> 01:04:10,461
- It's for your fare.
- That's alright.

589
01:04:10,462 --> 01:04:11,486
You act so cool.

590
01:04:14,299 --> 01:04:17,826
How about betting bigger next time?

591
01:04:21,807 --> 01:04:22,807
Why not?

592
01:04:28,246 --> 01:04:31,079
You're dead meat!

593
01:04:34,953 --> 01:04:38,189
DANSOO [ATARI]: ONE MOVE AWAY
FROM BEING CAPTURED.

594
01:04:38,190 --> 01:04:43,194
It's what I do.
Our target market is China.

595
01:04:43,195 --> 01:04:46,221
It's the second biggest
movie market.

596
01:04:53,505 --> 01:04:54,995
Care for a sneak peek?

597
01:04:55,273 --> 01:04:56,501
Let's start the game.

598
01:04:57,275 --> 01:04:58,833
- Right away?
- Sure.

599
01:04:59,144 --> 01:05:01,442
I gotta take a leak first.

600
01:05:01,513 --> 01:05:05,506
Try this in your mouth.
It feels good!

601
01:05:41,153 --> 01:05:44,850
This business is in recession, too.

602
01:05:44,923 --> 01:05:49,794
People watch porn on their phones
nowadays. So it doesn't earn any money.

603
01:05:49,795 --> 01:05:54,532
Movies gotta have soul in it.

604
01:05:54,533 --> 01:05:57,968
But it's all about moaning now.

605
01:05:57,969 --> 01:05:59,664
What will the youngsters
learn from it?

606
01:06:00,072 --> 01:06:06,272
I can't help but worry
about this country's future.

607
01:06:23,128 --> 01:06:25,396
Are you OK with this location?

608
01:06:25,397 --> 01:06:28,699
I feel bad that I chose
my home grounds.

609
01:06:28,700 --> 01:06:34,004
- Let's keep it quiet.
- This is how I loosen up.

610
01:06:34,005 --> 01:06:36,874
- How about having a smoke?
- I quit.

611
01:06:36,875 --> 01:06:41,679
The human lung is such a delicate organ,
that can be compared to a lotus...

612
01:06:41,680 --> 01:06:43,648
Keep your mouth shut, I said.

613
01:06:58,797 --> 01:07:01,732
Oh my God, what's this?

614
01:07:01,733 --> 01:07:03,963
I thought I lost but
I won by one and a half points?

615
01:07:06,705 --> 01:07:09,469
I will keep this in custody.
It's heavy.

616
01:07:13,378 --> 01:07:14,675
Show some respect, dude.

617
01:07:14,846 --> 01:07:16,480
How much did you lose?

618
01:07:16,481 --> 01:07:17,382
Two large bills.

619
01:07:17,383 --> 01:07:19,714
How large?
2 million?

620
01:07:20,986 --> 01:07:23,888
Since when did you become

621
01:07:23,889 --> 01:07:27,791
such a pushover?

622
01:07:28,560 --> 01:07:30,391
Don't get on my nerves.

623
01:07:32,964 --> 01:07:37,168
There's a saying, "man is most 
prideful just before he falls."

624
01:07:37,169 --> 01:07:39,160
Never let down your guard
at this level of play!

625
01:07:39,938 --> 01:07:41,071
Shut up and help me tomorrow.

626
01:07:41,072 --> 01:07:45,576
By the way...
Does Killer know about this?

627
01:07:45,577 --> 01:07:47,545
Don't wag your tongue.

628
01:07:47,546 --> 01:07:48,979
What's the split?

629
01:07:48,980 --> 01:07:50,881
60, 40 as always.

630
01:07:50,882 --> 01:07:51,882
Let's do 50, 50.

631
01:07:53,652 --> 01:07:54,852
Are you trying to negotiate with me?

632
01:07:54,853 --> 01:07:58,220
Well, I'm not the one who's 
got his back to the edge.

633
01:07:59,591 --> 01:08:01,559
Greedy men never
age gracefully.

634
01:08:07,065 --> 01:08:10,831
If you look at me like that again,
I'll kill you myself.

635
01:08:19,611 --> 01:08:22,446
- You don't have to count?
- No need.

636
01:08:22,447 --> 01:08:25,382
It feels better to count at home.

637
01:08:25,383 --> 01:08:27,442
You won't have to do
any counting today.

638
01:08:34,159 --> 01:08:37,494
It's <i>Dansoo, Atari</i>!

639
01:08:37,495 --> 01:08:40,623
I can see.
Shut your mouth.

640
01:08:40,932 --> 01:08:45,392
Who's this bastard?
He's not taking the bait!

641
01:08:51,509 --> 01:08:52,509
<i>On 5 and 9.</i>

642
01:08:58,917 --> 01:09:00,748
Don't blow smoke in my face.

643
01:09:06,491 --> 01:09:11,827
Tons of trick moves...
I recognize this playstyle.

644
01:09:12,297 --> 01:09:15,528
Long time no see, you kibitzer.

645
01:09:16,134 --> 01:09:20,002
Take the bait,
you son of a bitch!

646
01:09:28,647 --> 01:09:31,275
Bastards!

647
01:09:35,754 --> 01:09:38,155
Didn't you quit?

648
01:09:38,156 --> 01:09:41,557
I quit quitting.
I got dumped by a chick.

649
01:09:42,427 --> 01:09:44,759
I'm getting curious
how big your mouth can get.

650
01:09:46,298 --> 01:09:51,769
This son of a bitch!
Now he's playing me?

651
01:09:51,770 --> 01:09:53,635
Player, on 6 and 4.

652
01:09:55,840 --> 01:09:56,898
He's pushing forward.

653
01:09:58,843 --> 01:10:01,779
Women are scary creatures.

654
01:10:01,780 --> 01:10:04,481
We were together for so long

655
01:10:04,482 --> 01:10:06,617
but she cut me off just like that.

656
01:10:06,618 --> 01:10:10,281
Quite similar to Go.
When they cut you off,

657
01:10:11,356 --> 01:10:13,449
This motherfucker
is totally playing me!

658
01:10:13,725 --> 01:10:15,249
They do so mercilessly.

659
01:10:20,398 --> 01:10:23,434
<i>They're messing with us!</i>

660
01:10:23,435 --> 01:10:28,771
<i>Screw the game!
You hear me? Screw it!</i>

661
01:10:29,574 --> 01:10:32,975
What the hell!

662
01:10:47,492 --> 01:10:52,657
Please don't kill me!
I beg you.

663
01:10:56,935 --> 01:10:58,562
I better get a big bonus for this!

664
01:11:03,341 --> 01:11:06,071
I don't remember inviting you.

665
01:11:06,411 --> 01:11:07,571
Use the dagger, if you want.

666
01:11:18,356 --> 01:11:21,052
Came for a brain game
but forced to use brawn.

667
01:11:21,459 --> 01:11:23,188
Brawn is a part of Go, too.

668
01:11:50,989 --> 01:11:52,456
Beat him to death!

669
01:12:10,608 --> 01:12:12,168
I'll have to let you
play alone, Player.

670
01:12:30,762 --> 01:12:32,389
What the hell!

671
01:12:41,139 --> 01:12:42,231
Hold on tight!

672
01:13:00,258 --> 01:13:04,217
SPIN AROUND ATTACK:
ATTACKING BY SERIES OF FATAL MOVES

673
01:13:10,502 --> 01:13:11,594
The rules are simple.

674
01:13:13,171 --> 01:13:15,230
The winner gets out.

675
01:13:23,014 --> 01:13:24,572
What's all this about?

676
01:13:25,750 --> 01:13:27,510
Let's play a quick game
before we freeze.

677
01:13:28,419 --> 01:13:33,288
You should play a move before
the sand runs out. Your move.

678
01:13:36,294 --> 01:13:37,556
Come on!

679
01:14:54,472 --> 01:14:56,152
Look at the winter swagger
frozen to death.

680
01:14:59,077 --> 01:15:01,204
Look at the true dandy
stabbed to death!

681
01:15:06,351 --> 01:15:09,912
This is a <i>tsumego</i>.
One move to make the group live.

682
01:15:11,322 --> 01:15:13,256
That's the padlock code.

683
01:15:49,794 --> 01:15:52,991
I need a drink.
A warm one.

684
01:15:59,971 --> 01:16:01,632
You look terrible.

685
01:16:02,006 --> 01:16:03,473
How about a game?

686
01:16:05,209 --> 01:16:07,473
For fun or for a bet?

687
01:16:19,323 --> 01:16:21,416
Well, you'll get more fun
by betting something.

688
01:16:22,326 --> 01:16:23,623
What should the bet be?

689
01:16:28,700 --> 01:16:29,724
Granting a wish?

690
01:16:32,270 --> 01:16:33,328
Too childish.

691
01:16:35,440 --> 01:16:37,567
Childish, but of tradition.

692
01:16:38,676 --> 01:16:42,012
This is a unique board.
Are they goddesses?

693
01:16:42,013 --> 01:16:45,540
Goddess of fortune and
goddess of destruction.

694
01:16:47,919 --> 01:16:51,616
- Which one am I?
- Destruction suits you.

695
01:16:53,157 --> 01:16:55,455
The width of the board is 45 centimeters.

696
01:16:56,661 --> 01:16:59,630
The perfect distance
for sharing feelings.

697
01:17:01,265 --> 01:17:02,857
How can people
share their feelings?

698
01:17:03,067 --> 01:17:06,093
It would be like
making you mine.

699
01:17:07,238 --> 01:17:08,238
Dansoo.

700
01:17:09,674 --> 01:17:11,164
I won't be easy.

701
01:17:16,180 --> 01:17:17,180
Good move.

702
01:17:19,484 --> 01:17:20,883
I was just lucky.

703
01:17:30,061 --> 01:17:32,154
Be careful what you wish for.

704
01:18:09,567 --> 01:18:11,368
You're definitely
getting my attention.

705
01:18:11,369 --> 01:18:13,530
How about a game?

706
01:18:14,739 --> 01:18:16,540
It'd be exciting
to put our lives on the line.

707
01:18:16,541 --> 01:18:19,943
I like it.
<i>Can't wait to see you.</i>

708
01:18:19,944 --> 01:18:23,680
I left you a gift
at the calligraphy academy.

709
01:18:23,681 --> 01:18:25,308
Also, turn off the freezer.

710
01:18:25,917 --> 01:18:27,316
And open the cabinet.

711
01:18:28,286 --> 01:18:29,310
Open the cabinet!

712
01:18:45,136 --> 01:18:46,136
Untie him.

713
01:18:52,643 --> 01:18:55,134
What took you so long?
Hurry!

714
01:18:56,581 --> 01:18:58,173
<i>Log on with ID: Master Wang
PW: QWER34</i>

715
01:18:59,250 --> 01:19:02,083
Boss, I saw him!

716
01:19:05,423 --> 01:19:06,423
Sit here.

717
01:19:07,925 --> 01:19:09,192
Let go of me, bastards.

718
01:19:09,193 --> 01:19:11,828
What's going on?
I didn't do anything!

719
01:19:11,829 --> 01:19:15,595
Player forced me to do it!
I didn't steal the money!

720
01:19:20,771 --> 01:19:23,707
<i>6 million is my bet. I need
his tongue as yours.</i>

721
01:19:23,708 --> 01:19:27,677
Do not listen to him.
I'll pay off the shortfall.

722
01:19:27,678 --> 01:19:30,413
We're partners!

723
01:19:30,414 --> 01:19:32,848
Don't be foolish!

724
01:19:33,284 --> 01:19:35,364
<i>CARPE DIEM requested a game.
Press ACCEPT or DECLINE.</i>

725
01:19:36,387 --> 01:19:40,517
Please, don't do this to me!

726
01:19:41,959 --> 01:19:42,959
Accept it.

727
01:19:43,527 --> 01:19:44,960
It's a trap!

728
01:19:46,430 --> 01:19:47,430
I told you to accept.

729
01:19:51,068 --> 01:19:55,937
Good, I will crush this bastard!

730
01:20:19,430 --> 01:20:21,455
Got a cigarette?

731
01:20:40,251 --> 01:20:46,815
Do you know why I like Go
of all the games?

732
01:20:47,658 --> 01:20:52,322
Because it's a brain game.
Petty tricks don't work.

733
01:20:52,430 --> 01:20:55,732
It's the smart ones who win.

734
01:20:55,733 --> 01:20:58,600
Isn't it beautifully simple?

735
01:21:02,606 --> 01:21:06,440
Give me some water, assholes!

736
01:21:39,310 --> 01:21:41,107
<i>Point counting requested.</i>

737
01:21:45,116 --> 01:21:46,116
Accept.

738
01:21:53,824 --> 01:21:55,824
<i>Congratulations!
White won by half a point.</i>

739
01:21:59,330 --> 01:22:00,524
<i>Still reviewing the game?</i>

740
01:22:00,631 --> 01:22:02,895
<i>Flip the goban on the table over.</i>

741
01:22:03,434 --> 01:22:04,731
Flip it over.

742
01:22:10,608 --> 01:22:13,236
<i>See the hole?
It's called the "blood flow".</i>

743
01:22:15,012 --> 01:22:18,675
<i>It's a hole to fill with the blood
from the Master's tongue.</i>

744
01:22:22,353 --> 01:22:26,414
Please, I will get him.
I promise!

745
01:22:27,291 --> 01:22:28,815
I will get him to you!

746
01:22:31,328 --> 01:22:36,265
I'll get him!
Please don't do that!

747
01:22:47,511 --> 01:22:49,479
<i>Evil leaves the mouth...</i>

748
01:23:03,394 --> 01:23:05,154
<i>By the way, the window sign
is missing a letter.</i>

749
01:23:35,159 --> 01:23:38,761
It smells fantastic!
Is it cooked yet?

750
01:23:38,762 --> 01:23:41,629
Come on, Big Move!
Let's have a feast!

751
01:23:42,800 --> 01:23:45,860
Do you guys know why I play Go?

752
01:23:46,437 --> 01:23:51,101
Confucius once said, "It's better
to play Go than to do nothing all day."

753
01:23:53,177 --> 01:23:55,805
You should listen to the sages.

754
01:23:57,548 --> 01:24:02,451
Christ, how did you become a Master 
without being able to see?

755
01:24:02,553 --> 01:24:05,386
Give us the secret!

756
01:24:06,624 --> 01:24:08,649
I looked over others' shoulders.

757
01:24:14,231 --> 01:24:19,134
Seriously, come on!
I want to know the secret!

758
01:24:19,236 --> 01:24:24,299
When I was selling junk
on the street,

759
01:24:24,875 --> 01:24:26,740
someone came to me.

760
01:24:27,111 --> 01:24:31,775
He told me he'd seen me before.
And he invited me to play Go.

761
01:24:32,750 --> 01:24:36,319
I told him I couldn't play
because I'm blind.

762
01:24:36,320 --> 01:24:38,481
Then he gave me a present.

763
01:24:39,223 --> 01:24:41,657
Stones for the blind.

764
01:24:41,725 --> 01:24:46,526
We played Go every day.

765
01:24:46,897 --> 01:24:49,933
He was a true master.
A real one.

766
01:24:49,934 --> 01:24:55,270
And after exactly one year,
he stopped showing up.

767
01:24:58,809 --> 01:25:02,301
He might be the one who
told me about you.

768
01:25:04,949 --> 01:25:06,473
Have you seen him?

769
01:25:08,018 --> 01:25:09,417
No.

770
01:25:10,087 --> 01:25:13,022
When I was in solitary confinement,

771
01:25:13,023 --> 01:25:17,483
we used to play Go, banging
on the walls. I lost every time.

772
01:25:29,240 --> 01:25:32,698
Who's there?
Tell me who you are!

773
01:25:33,444 --> 01:25:36,679
But there was no chalk

774
01:25:36,680 --> 01:25:39,282
in his cell.

775
01:25:39,283 --> 01:25:44,954
It's simple.
He never marked anything.

776
01:25:44,955 --> 01:25:47,219
You mean he played
blind Go?

777
01:25:47,725 --> 01:25:52,895
He played the entire game in his head
and beat Big Move? Impossible.

778
01:25:52,896 --> 01:25:58,198
I heard that there's a 
player like this in Busan.

779
01:25:58,802 --> 01:26:03,466
They call him the Ghost.

780
01:26:03,574 --> 01:26:05,439
Ghost?

781
01:26:17,955 --> 01:26:25,955
Cheater, do you have a minute?
Please do me a favor.

782
01:26:26,063 --> 01:26:28,398
I won't buy drinks for you.

783
01:26:28,399 --> 01:26:29,730
I quit drinking.

784
01:26:31,235 --> 01:26:34,037
Next you'll tell 
me you can see.

785
01:26:34,038 --> 01:26:35,505
What do you want?

786
01:26:47,985 --> 01:26:52,581
Christ, you're damn good looking!
You blushed.

787
01:26:54,458 --> 01:26:55,891
It's too funny.

788
01:27:08,539 --> 01:27:14,774
Oh my God!
Chicks will be all over you!

789
01:27:18,182 --> 01:27:22,118
Don't worry so much.

790
01:27:22,119 --> 01:27:23,450
Your daughter must be glad.

791
01:27:36,367 --> 01:27:38,858
Well... it seems like
we need to run.

792
01:27:43,574 --> 01:27:44,700
This way!

793
01:27:47,711 --> 01:27:49,645
Wait.

794
01:27:53,250 --> 01:27:55,810
You damn bastard.

795
01:27:57,921 --> 01:28:00,287
Not today!
It's a big day for us!

796
01:28:06,730 --> 01:28:07,730
Bring it on!

797
01:28:12,336 --> 01:28:13,736
WEAK GROUP: ENDANGERED STONES
SURROUNDED BY THE OPPONENT

798
01:28:13,737 --> 01:28:19,505
What a surprise, that we 
should meet again like this.

799
01:28:21,245 --> 01:28:23,406
I've prepared a fun game.

800
01:28:24,982 --> 01:28:30,153
One of my men died
because he couldn't solve

801
01:28:30,154 --> 01:28:31,314
this <i>tsumego</i>.

802
01:28:33,757 --> 01:28:35,019
You will have three chances.

803
01:28:36,226 --> 01:28:40,526
Can I play seated?
I think my toes are broken.

804
01:28:45,736 --> 01:28:48,204
Game on.

805
01:29:12,696 --> 01:29:13,696
Two chances left.

806
01:29:13,964 --> 01:29:16,532
Please have mercy.

807
01:29:16,533 --> 01:29:18,398
Game on again.

808
01:29:45,062 --> 01:29:46,062
Last chance.

809
01:30:07,851 --> 01:30:11,981
Please, I beg you.

810
01:30:15,926 --> 01:30:17,120
I guess it's your lucky day.

811
01:30:30,274 --> 01:30:31,935
Rest in peace, my love.

812
01:30:33,610 --> 01:30:37,680
I recognize you now.
I thought I killed you.

813
01:30:37,681 --> 01:30:41,617
I was dead, but now I'm born again.
I'll change your fate, too.

814
01:30:41,985 --> 01:30:46,922
The bet is 6 million on top of
your buddy's head.

815
01:30:47,391 --> 01:30:50,326
I can't wait to see who will win.

816
01:30:53,196 --> 01:30:57,496
Try your damn best.
Your life is on it.

817
01:30:58,502 --> 01:31:02,529
How about betting
my life instead of his?

818
01:31:04,241 --> 01:31:05,241
Christ...

819
01:31:05,642 --> 01:31:09,738
Cheer up.
We'll have a drink after this game.

820
01:31:14,084 --> 01:31:18,748
But I don't have stones
for the blind here.

821
01:31:23,961 --> 01:31:25,189
I will play the blind Go.

822
01:31:25,762 --> 01:31:27,830
No, Christ, you shouldn't!

823
01:31:27,831 --> 01:31:28,831
Blind Go?

824
01:31:31,168 --> 01:31:33,466
No, you can't!

825
01:31:34,004 --> 01:31:40,000
- You should help me.
- Christ, please don't!

826
01:31:45,716 --> 01:31:46,740
Playing a blind game?

827
01:31:46,917 --> 01:31:50,978
Why?
You can't beat a blind man?

828
01:31:54,524 --> 01:31:58,290
I'll show mercy, and end
your life as fast as I can.

829
01:32:02,599 --> 01:32:04,089
Star point on upper left corner.

830
01:32:13,944 --> 01:32:18,313
Strong opening for an old man.
Quite provocative.

831
01:32:33,163 --> 01:32:34,830
Low 3-4 point on lower left corner.

832
01:32:34,831 --> 01:32:38,858
I can't fight
against an elder.

833
01:32:42,973 --> 01:32:43,997
I'll dodge.

834
01:32:44,374 --> 01:32:46,001
Opposite 3-4 point
on upper right corner.

835
01:32:47,811 --> 01:32:49,278
Star point on lower right corner.

836
01:32:54,084 --> 01:32:55,517
Starting the fight so soon?

837
01:32:59,556 --> 01:33:01,649
Right 3-4 point on upper right corner.

838
01:33:03,460 --> 01:33:05,027
I don't want to fight.

839
01:33:05,028 --> 01:33:08,987
I'll cut your throat if I win.

840
01:33:09,733 --> 01:33:11,633
Knight's approach
on upper right corner.

841
01:33:19,643 --> 01:33:22,635
Don't fight back.
Large Knight on upper right corner.

842
01:33:23,046 --> 01:33:31,046
As you like.
I'll go my own way.

843
01:33:31,822 --> 01:33:34,347
Large Knight stretched
on lower left corner.

844
01:33:34,691 --> 01:33:37,592
Lower Pincer by 3 spaces
on upper right corner.

845
01:33:39,463 --> 01:33:43,832
You're scaring me. I'll run away.

846
01:33:44,334 --> 01:33:46,495
Center, cover the cap.

847
01:33:53,810 --> 01:33:55,334
On 10 and 10.
Dodge.

848
01:33:55,712 --> 01:33:58,203
He's the one who struggles,
not us.

849
01:34:02,953 --> 01:34:04,053
Diamond on the zenith.

850
01:34:04,054 --> 01:34:06,887
Choke lower side by a territory.

851
01:34:09,226 --> 01:34:12,389
Knight's move
on right side of center. Attack now.

852
01:34:18,168 --> 01:34:19,692
Knight's move
on left side of center.

853
01:34:30,547 --> 01:34:32,572
On 14 and 13. Cut it!

854
01:34:36,453 --> 01:34:44,453
Got him!
We got him!

855
01:34:45,428 --> 01:34:47,919
You're dead meat, motherfucker!

856
01:34:53,403 --> 01:34:54,403
On 7 and 7.

857
01:34:55,572 --> 01:34:57,836
- He just cut it.
- Move forward!

858
01:35:00,143 --> 01:35:02,373
You better be ready to die.

859
01:35:48,391 --> 01:35:52,623
A scumbag like you
couldn't play like that.

860
01:35:53,196 --> 01:35:55,289
Nice moves...
for a blind man.

861
01:35:59,102 --> 01:36:00,729
Listen, Cheater.

862
01:36:03,607 --> 01:36:06,838
The world isn't a playground to me.

863
01:36:07,878 --> 01:36:14,306
I'm sorry.
The drinks should wait.

864
01:36:37,941 --> 01:36:39,772
Review the game in your grave.

865
01:37:07,971 --> 01:37:10,269
I nailed Drinking Christ to the board.
Sorry.

866
01:37:12,042 --> 01:37:15,945
If you win,
I will spare his life.

867
01:37:15,946 --> 01:37:22,010
Big Move... Don't worry.
I can't make it anyways.

868
01:37:23,053 --> 01:37:27,353
- I will come back.
- No, don't!

869
01:37:56,119 --> 01:38:02,149
Don't play the game.
You can't win.

870
01:38:03,727 --> 01:38:11,065
He can't be beaten. The moves
are too subtle.

871
01:38:13,003 --> 01:38:19,909
It must be a kid playing.
An innocent one.

872
01:38:41,364 --> 01:38:43,958
You better do your best
if you want a happy ending.

873
01:38:46,469 --> 01:38:47,509
Keep the kid out of this.

874
01:38:50,640 --> 01:38:53,404
- Kill them both if I lose.
- Yes, sir.

875
01:38:58,481 --> 01:39:01,473
How many handicaps would you take
if you played against the god of Go?

876
01:39:01,818 --> 01:39:02,818
Two.

877
01:39:03,887 --> 01:39:07,050
- If your life's on it?
- Three.

878
01:39:08,058 --> 01:39:13,052
If there is a god of Go,
it must be a child, right?

879
01:39:14,397 --> 01:39:15,591
Stop here.

880
01:39:17,000 --> 01:39:19,798
- Are you scared of me?
- You'll never win.

881
01:39:32,115 --> 01:39:36,051
LIFE AND DEATH:
ONE MOVE TO STAY ALIVE

882
01:40:00,477 --> 01:40:01,808
Kill the Carpenter.

883
01:40:15,458 --> 01:40:17,585
Same opening as the blind man.

884
01:40:22,198 --> 01:40:29,969
3-3 point? Not very much 
influence, playing in the corner.

885
01:40:30,440 --> 01:40:31,907
Cover on the star point.

886
01:40:44,120 --> 01:40:48,113
Double 3-3 point?
You're too defensive.

887
01:40:56,266 --> 01:41:00,430
Can we start the fight already?

888
01:41:07,377 --> 01:41:10,403
Come with us.

889
01:41:12,649 --> 01:41:15,948
Let me see if there's 
a way out for me, first.

890
01:41:20,390 --> 01:41:23,223
Life and death
is always difficult.

891
01:41:24,694 --> 01:41:28,755
That's why it starts the fight.

892
01:41:32,302 --> 01:41:34,133
Let's see who lives
and who dies.

893
01:41:35,338 --> 01:41:39,832
You'll regret it.
I'll make it painful.

894
01:42:15,945 --> 01:42:18,209
Are you throwing a stone,
or making a move?

895
01:42:18,615 --> 01:42:19,615
It's a move.

896
01:42:21,317 --> 01:42:26,050
Did you know that she dies if you win?

897
01:42:34,931 --> 01:42:37,764
Don't even think about it.
What're you waiting for?

898
01:43:19,542 --> 01:43:23,137
On 8 and 10, cap on center.
Attack.

899
01:43:55,511 --> 01:43:58,878
He made the losing move.
<i>On 1 and 2, move forward.</i>

900
01:44:07,890 --> 01:44:09,858
On 3 and 3, connect.

901
01:44:22,739 --> 01:44:24,969
On 4 and 1.
<i>Bend.</i>

902
01:44:35,385 --> 01:44:38,787
It's Eternal Life.
We're even.

903
01:44:38,788 --> 01:44:40,551
We can play forever
or you can yield.

904
01:44:57,740 --> 01:44:59,469
What if I don't want to yield?

905
01:45:04,080 --> 01:45:05,240
Then we're even.

906
01:45:11,320 --> 01:45:14,915
Being even isn't part of my plan.

907
01:45:15,425 --> 01:45:17,393
Then we should
finish this here.

908
01:45:22,565 --> 01:45:26,296
Interesting.
It doesn't get better than this.

909
01:45:27,437 --> 01:45:28,563
Bring the bitch.

910
01:45:39,715 --> 01:45:41,239
How do we end this?

911
01:45:42,118 --> 01:45:47,989
Have you seen all the stones
on the board disappear?

912
01:45:47,990 --> 01:45:51,084
Take a close look.
You'll witness that.

913
01:47:08,838 --> 01:47:10,872
Wearing protection?

914
01:47:10,873 --> 01:47:13,103
How manly...

915
01:50:46,756 --> 01:50:51,056
SCORING: END THE GAME 
AND CALL THE VICTOR

916
01:50:51,794 --> 01:50:53,523
I worked for your father.

917
01:50:54,430 --> 01:50:57,126
He left something for you.

918
01:51:26,629 --> 01:51:27,629
How have you been?

919
01:51:37,573 --> 01:51:44,137
Keep this.
And call me three times a day.

920
01:52:05,835 --> 01:52:07,496
Isn't it too cold out?

921
01:52:12,908 --> 01:52:14,341
My hands are warm as ever.

922
01:52:15,377 --> 01:52:17,512
Christ once asked me

923
01:52:17,513 --> 01:52:19,708
if there's a divine move in life.

924
01:52:21,317 --> 01:52:25,185
I now understand
there's no such move.

925
01:52:25,588 --> 01:52:31,356
The best move we can make
is to live every day.

926
01:53:38,961 --> 01:53:40,656
Where are we heading now?

927
01:53:41,463 --> 01:53:42,521
To Busan.

928
01:53:51,941 --> 01:53:57,243
THE DIVINE MOVE
Life and Death

929
01:53:59,181 --> 01:54:01,342
Directed by JO Bum-go

